---
title: Choose Your Deck
bg: landing
description: A fan-made Yu-Gi-Oh! guide covering multiple Ritual and combo decks and engines. Mitsurugi and Fiendsmith are live now, Sacred Beasts is in progress, plus a shared Handtraps reference.
---
{% from "components.njk" import bossArt, synergyCard %}

{# The header and the grid it introduces are one section. As two sections they
   were 96px apart while the grid sat only 48px from the next section down, so
   the page's biggest gap fell inside a group and its smallest between them. #}
<section class="container section-pad-lg">
  <div class="section-head-center">
    <div class="kicker">// {{ site.neutralWordmark }}</div>
    <h1>Choose your deck.</h1>
    <p>One guide, more than one grind. Pick a deck or engine below for its full card compendium and combo lines.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="deck-grid">
    {% for d in hub.decks %}
    <a class="boss-card" href="{{ d.href | url }}" style="--card-accent:{{ d.accent }};">
      {{ bossArt(d) }}
      <div class="boss-body">
        {# h2, not h3: the deck names are this page's primary content and they
           come before the only other h2 ("Shared reference"), so an h3 here
           made the hub's outline read h1 → h3 → h2. #}
        <h2>{{ d.name }}{% if d.status == "wip" %} <span class="wip-badge">WIP</span>{% endif %}</h2>
        <div class="boss-stat">{{ d.tagline }}</div>
        <div class="boss-desc">{{ d.body }}</div>
        {# Names the three-page shape before the reader commits, which also makes
           the header's per-deck dropdown discoverable by implication. Not links:
           the whole card is already one, and nesting anchors is invalid. #}
        <div class="boss-pages mono">Overview · Cards · Combos</div>
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Shared reference</h2>
    <p class="prose">Not every card belongs to one deck. Handtraps get one shared page instead of being copy-pasted onto each deck's compendium.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="synergy-grid">
    {% for e in hub.engines %}
    {{ synergyCard(e) }}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

{# The page's closing aside: whose notebook this is and why it's public. Heading
   left, note right, so it reads as an afterword rather than a fourth thing to
   pick off the hub. #}
<section class="container section">
  <div class="two-col note">
    <h2>Why does this site exist?</h2>
    <div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Honestly: for me. I've been playing Yu-Gi-Oh! for about a year, and the fastest way I've found to actually learn a deck is to write it down. Every card sorted by where it activates, every combo line typed out step by step until the sequencing sticks in my head.</p>
        <p>So this is my notebook, made public. A deck is here because I wanted to pilot it and had to understand it first, and anything marked <strong>WIP</strong> is a deck I'm still learning.</p>
        <p>No ads, no wall of verbatim card text, no sign-up. If it helps you pick up a deck too, even better.</p>
      </div>
      {# Outside .prose: `.prose p + p` would outrank .note-sign's own margin. #}
      <p class="note-sign">Medonni</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
